1 Introduction
**************

‘polygram’ is a small, standard-library-only packaging and orchestration
layer that curates Claude agent skills driven by _tags in MEMORY_. Notes
captured the Mentat way accumulate tags; polygram reads those tags,
evaluates each candidate at a “gate”, synthesizes skill skeletons only
for the ones that pass, and mints installable bundles -- leaving a
growing on-disk history of “advice” behind every decision.

   polygram does not author skill content for quality; it governs which
themes become skills and packages the result.  Mentat is the note
discipline that feeds it, and skilltank is the eye that spots
skill-shaped patterns; polygram is the forge between them.


