2 Concepts
**********

“note”
     One fact in a Markdown file under ‘memory/’, optionally carrying
     tags.
“tag”
     A label attached to a note, either an Org-style heading tag (‘#
     Title :SKILL:’) or an inline hashtag (‘#shell-tooling’).
“control tag”
     ‘:SKILL:’, ‘#skill-candidate’, ‘#synth’.  These _promote a note's
     other tags_ rather than becoming skills themselves.
“candidate”
     A tag cluster, surfaced when it appears in enough notes (the
     ‘--threshold’, default 2) or is force-surfaced by a control tag.
“gate”
     The deterministic scorer that turns a candidate into a verdict.
“verdict”
     One of ‘PASS’, ‘HOLD’, ‘REJECT’, with its reasoning.
“advice”
     The dated Markdown record of a verdict, written under ‘advice/’.


