4 The pipeline
**************

The core loop is
     notes -> candidates -> gate (PASS/HOLD/REJECT) -> advice -> synthesis -> dist

4.1 The gate
============

Each candidate is scored on cheap, explainable signals:

Signal                                             Effect
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
corroborated by two or more notes                  +2
explicitly flagged by the operator                 surfaces only (no
                                                   score)
well-formed label (an all-letter word, or a        +1
hyphenated label of 4+ characters)
overly generic label (‘misc’, ...)                 -2

   ‘PASS’ (score >= 3) synthesizes a skill skeleton; ‘HOLD’ (>= 1)
records advice and waits for review; ‘REJECT’ is logged and dropped.

4.2 Review
==========

A ‘HOLD’ verdict parks a candidate that lacks the signal to auto-pass.
Work the queue with ‘polygram review’: ‘--promote’ overrides the gate
and synthesizes, ‘--reject’ records a rejection, and ‘--freeze-extern’
pins the upstream a held candidate came from.


