5 Distribution
**************

‘polygram dist’ packages curated skills.  It gathers the workspace
‘skills/’ plus any installed sources, writes a ‘MANIFEST’ with a SHA-256
per file, and mints archives.

‘--format tar.gz|zip|skill|both|all’
     ‘both’ (default) mints ‘.tar.gz’ and ‘.zip’; ‘skill’ mints a
     folder-rooted, installable ‘<name>.skill’ per skill; ‘all’ mints
     everything.
‘--skills-source DIR’
     An installed-skills root to include (repeatable).  When omitted,
     polygram reads ‘POLYGRAM_SKILLS_SOURCE’ (an ‘os.pathsep’-separated
     list).
‘--all-installed’
     Include all installed skills, not just the Mentat-family allowlist.
‘--name NAME / --dist-version VERSION / --out DIR’
     Archive base name, version stamp, and output directory.

   On a name collision the workspace copy wins.  Editor and build cruft
(‘__pycache__’, ‘*.pyc’, ‘*~’, ‘*.tmp’, Emacs ‘#autosave#’, ‘.git’,
‘.DS_Store’) is excluded from every archive and bundle.


File: polygram.info,  Node: Externs,  Next: Command reference,  Prev: Distribution,  Up: Top

6 Externs
*********

An “extern” is an upstream skill source cloned under ‘externs/<name>/’
and recorded in ‘externs.json’.  An extern feeds candidates _only
through its own ‘memory/’ notes_, never arbitrary documents in the
cloned repository -- this prevents upstream noise from surfacing as
skills.

   An extern has a “kind”: ‘git’ (a cloned remote) or ‘local’ (a
hand-authored snapshot with no remote).  “Freezing” pins an extern at a
revision so ‘polygram extern sync’ skips it, and a held candidate from a
frozen extern is flagged during review.


