8 Quality control
*****************

Synthesized skeletons are drafts, not shippable skills.  polygram's
practice is to pass them through a “sub-agent quality-control gate”:
independent reviewers -- a skill-builder reviewer (skill-creator and
skilltank conventions) and an SRE reviewer (provenance and safe-tooling)
-- judge each skeleton, and a skill ships only when both agree it is
skill-shaped and sound.

   This gate is what distinguishes a real skill from noise.  In the
2026-06-27 cycle it shipped ‘color-theory’ (a WCAG contrast tool),
rejected ‘concise’ (a preference, not a procedure), and rejected
‘ffcc00’ (a colour token scraped from an upstream's diagrams) -- then
the extern was frozen and a hex-token guard added so the noise could not
recur.


